{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>Woe to you, Moav.</b> All this is from the proverb." "<b>You are lost, O people of Kemosh.</b> For you are lost and driven from the world, you, Moav, the people of Kemosh, in the exile of Sichon. And do not wonder at the word אבדת, for its meaning is nifal, like ״אבד חסיד מן הארץ״, which means nifal." "<b>He gave his sons as fugitives.</b> It means הניח, left — like ״ולא נתן סיחון״. That is, the rest of his small sons of Moav, who were fugitives from the sword of Sichon, and his daughters, whose way is not to fight — he left them <b>in captivity to the king of the Amorites, Sichon,</b> for he could not save them from his hand."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:08.854418762Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}